 "notes": "First Parkes Pulsar Polarization Array (PPPA) search for ultralight axion-like dark matter via the ALDM Chern-Simons (axion-photon) coupling g_agamma inducing cosmic-birefringence oscillation of pulsar polarization position angles, using 22 MSPs from PPTA DR3. Curve traced from Fig. 2 (constraint_main.pdf in e-print), the solid red 'Full-corr' curve = full-correlation signal model WITH ionospheric subtraction, which is the paper's headline limit (dashed red = without ionospheric subtraction; blue = autocorrelation-only, presented as reference to show the crucial role of cross-correlation). Values recovered from the vector PDF via pymupdf get_drawings, calibrated to log-log axes (x: log10(m_a/eV), decades at px 103.1/189.5/275.9/362.3/448.7; y: log10(g_agamma/GeV^-1), decades at px 51.5..346.3, 58.96 px/decade). Cross-check: at m_a=1e-22 eV the traced value g~3.4e-14 (10^-13.5) matches the abstract's quoted 10^-13.5 to 10^-12.2 GeV^-1 over 10^-22 to 10^-21 eV. 95% upper limits. Benchmark local DM density rho_0 = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 (limit scales as rho_0^-1/2); not rescaled per task card. Full plotted mass range ~3e-24 to 3e-19 eV reported; limit weakens as m_a^2 above 1/T_obs.",
